# =============================================================================
# Stokowski — example .env
# =============================================================================
#
# Copy to `.env` in the directory you'll invoke `stokowski` from. The CLI
# loads `.env` from cwd before anything else; values below override shell
# env vars.
#
# Nothing here is interpreted by Stokowski itself. These are examples of
# variables your workflow.yaml may reference (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# LINEAR_API_KEY, …) via `tracker.api_key`, or pass through to agent
# subprocesses via `docker.extra_env`.
# =============================================================================

# ── Choosing a workflow file ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Pass a path, or let the CLI find one:
#
#   stokowski workflow.yaml     explicit
#   stokowski                   auto-detect: ./workflow.yaml, then
#                               ./workflow.yml, then ./WORKFLOW.md
#
# An explicit path always wins. There is no environment variable for this —
# STOKOWSKI_WORKFLOW_PATH was removed along with the multi-file discovery it
# fed. N projects now live in the `projects:` block of a single file.

# ── Workflow file (docker compose) ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# compose mounts one file to /app/workflow.yaml and passes that path on the
# command line. This controls the HOST side of that mount.
#
# Unset → ./workflow.yaml
# STOKOWSKI_WORKFLOW_HOST_PATH=./workflow.yaml


# ── Credentials referenced from workflow.yaml via $VAR ──────────────────────
# LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_your_key_here
# ALPHA_LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_alpha_team_key
# BETA_LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_beta_team_key

# ── Credentials passed to Docker-mode agent containers ──────────────────────
# Required for Claude Code inside containers (choose one):
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=your_generated_token_here

# Optional: GitHub token for agents that push PRs
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...
